<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nusrat Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1301">1301</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Nusrat Khan Jalesari</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nusrat Khan was a general and minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alauddin-khalji">Alauddin Khalji</a>, sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a>. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulugh-khan">Ulugh Khan</a> he led the invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> in 1299, sacking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patan-gujarat">Anahilavada</a> and the temple of Somnath and capturing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghel">Vaghela</a> queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamala-devi">Kamala Devi</a>. He was killed by a stone from a siege engine during the siege of Ranthambore in 1301.</p></div>
